@host = http://localhost:5187

# Authentication is faked from headers, so there is no token issuer to run. Send a subject and a
# space separated list of scopes; the tools name policies that require them.
@reader    = X-Demo-Subject: ada
@readScope = X-Demo-Scopes: tickets.read customers.read
@writer    = X-Demo-Scopes: tickets.read tickets.write customers.read
@admin     = X-Demo-Scopes: tickets.read tickets.write tickets.admin customers.read

### What this caller can do. Filtered and authorized exactly as the call is, so nothing listed
### here will then refuse them.
GET {{host}}/tools
{{reader}}
{{readScope}}

### The same question with no credentials at all. Comes back empty rather than refused, because a
### caller is never offered what they cannot invoke.
GET {{host}}/tools

### An admin sees more - including the destructive ones, which no reader is offered.
GET {{host}}/tools
{{reader}}
{{admin}}

### Narrowed to one surface. support_tickets_delete and support_tickets_purge declare themselves
### internal only, so they disappear from the MCP surface even for an admin.
GET {{host}}/tools?surface=mcp
{{reader}}
{{admin}}

### And on the internal surface they are back.
GET {{host}}/tools?surface=internal
{{reader}}
{{admin}}

### One declaration in full, schemas included. Note how the descriptions, the optionality and the
### enum's allowed values all come from the argument record.
GET {{host}}/tools/support_tickets_search
{{reader}}
{{readScope}}

### A tool that takes nothing.
POST {{host}}/tools/support_tickets_list
{{reader}}
{{readScope}}

### The same tool streamed, one JSON object per line. What a sequence tool is for.
POST {{host}}/tools/support_tickets_list/stream
{{reader}}
{{readScope}}

### Arguments go in the body, shaped by the input schema.
POST {{host}}/tools/support_tickets_search
Content-Type: application/json
{{reader}}
{{readScope}}

{ "query": "invoice", "status": "Pending", "limit": 5 }

### Reading one ticket in full.
POST {{host}}/tools/support_tickets_get
Content-Type: application/json
{{reader}}
{{readScope}}

{ "id": 1 }

### Arguments the schema rejects. Reported as something to correct rather than as a fault, so a
### model fixes them instead of retrying unchanged.
POST {{host}}/tools/support_tickets_search
Content-Type: application/json
{{reader}}
{{readScope}}

{ "limit": 500 }

### A write, refused: this caller holds tickets.read but not tickets.write.
POST {{host}}/tools/support_tickets_create
Content-Type: application/json
{{reader}}
{{readScope}}

{ "subject": "Cannot export", "body": "The CSV is empty.", "customerId": 1 }

### The same write, allowed.
POST {{host}}/tools/support_tickets_create
Content-Type: application/json
{{reader}}
{{writer}}

{ "subject": "Cannot export", "body": "The CSV is empty.", "customerId": 1 }

### A note. Not idempotent - calling it twice adds two notes, which is why the tool says so.
POST {{host}}/tools/support_notes_add
Content-Type: application/json
{{reader}}
{{writer}}

{ "ticketId": 1, "note": "Checked the mail relay logs." }

### Closing a ticket keeps it readable. Idempotent, so a retry is free.
POST {{host}}/tools/support_tickets_close
Content-Type: application/json
{{reader}}
{{writer}}

{ "id": 2, "resolution": "Refunded the duplicate charge." }

### A destructive tool on the surface it is declared for. Needs tickets.admin.
POST {{host}}/tools/support_tickets_delete?surface=internal
Content-Type: application/json
{{reader}}
{{admin}}

{ "id": 3 }

### The same call on the MCP surface. Reported as absent rather than refused, because from that
### surface it never existed - telling a model a tool exists but is barred invites it to keep asking.
POST {{host}}/tools/support_tickets_delete?surface=mcp
Content-Type: application/json
{{reader}}
{{admin}}

{ "id": 1 }

### A bulk destructive tool with a floor on what it will touch.
POST {{host}}/tools/support_tickets_purge?surface=internal
Content-Type: application/json
{{reader}}
{{admin}}

{ "olderThanDays": 60 }

### Below the floor, refused as an argument to correct.
POST {{host}}/tools/support_tickets_purge?surface=internal
Content-Type: application/json
{{reader}}
{{admin}}

{ "olderThanDays": 1 }

### Personal data. Labelled sensitivity=personal, which a policy could read without knowing what a
### customer is.
POST {{host}}/tools/support_customers_get
Content-Type: application/json
{{reader}}
{{readScope}}

{ "id": 1 }

### Open world: reaches a registry this application does not own, so it can fail for reasons no
### correct argument will fix.
POST {{host}}/tools/support_registry_lookup
Content-Type: application/json
{{reader}}
{{readScope}}

{ "companyName": "Northwind" }

### Not in the registry.
POST {{host}}/tools/support_registry_lookup
Content-Type: application/json
{{reader}}
{{readScope}}

{ "companyName": "Nowhere Ltd" }

### Read only, open world and NOT idempotent - calling it twice changes nothing but does not give
### the same answer twice, so a caller should not cache the first one.
POST {{host}}/tools/support_status_check
{{reader}}
{{readScope}}

### A tool with no class of its own: a delegate wrapped as an AIFunction, gated with
### RequireAuthorization at registration because there was no type to hang an attribute on.
POST {{host}}/tools/support_text_summarise
Content-Type: application/json
{{reader}}
{{readScope}}

{ "text": "The customer reports that the CSV export hangs at eighty percent and never completes." }

### A tool from a source this application does not control, renamed into a space of its own so a
### foreign "search" cannot shadow ours.
POST {{host}}/tools/support_kb_search
Content-Type: application/json
{{reader}}
{{readScope}}

{ "query": "password reset" }

### The third knowledge base tool describes itself with whitespace, so curation left it out rather
### than letting one bad foreign declaration stop the host. Watch the log for the warning.
POST {{host}}/tools/support_kb_retire
Content-Type: application/json
{{reader}}
{{admin}}

{ "id": "kb-1" }

### Deliberately not offered: marked [AgentToolIgnore], so assembly scanning passes over it.
POST {{host}}/tools/support_tickets_export
{{reader}}
{{admin}}

### A name nothing is declared under.
POST {{host}}/tools/support_tickets_obliterate
{{reader}}
{{admin}}
